\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Circuit diagram of the chaotic circuit. There are 6 op amps in total however LMC6062IN microchips were used. Each chip contained two op amps and the input and output of each op amp corresponding to specific pins on the chip. There are a total of 8 pins on the chip. Pin 3 and 5 corresponded to the non-inverting input of each op amp whereas pins 2 and 6 corresponded to the inverting input of each. Pins 1 and 7 were the output of the two op amps respectively. The three integrators are then the op amps with a $1\mu F$ capacitor placed in parallel, which are the 2nd op amp of the Chip 1 and both op amps in Chip 2. The final op amp, or the 2nd one in Chip 3 serves as a summing op amp.}}{8}{figure.caption.22}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:circuitdiagram}{{6}{8}{Circuit diagram of the chaotic circuit. There are 6 op amps in total however LMC6062IN microchips were used. Each chip contained two op amps and the input and output of each op amp corresponding to specific pins on the chip. There are a total of 8 pins on the chip. Pin 3 and 5 corresponded to the non-inverting input of each op amp whereas pins 2 and 6 corresponded to the inverting input of each. Pins 1 and 7 were the output of the two op amps respectively. The three integrators are then the op amps with a $1\mu F$ capacitor placed in parallel, which are the 2nd op amp of the Chip 1 and both op amps in Chip 2. The final op amp, or the 2nd one in Chip 3 serves as a summing op amp}{figure.caption.22}{}}
