\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces Graph displaying experimental measurement of the non-linear component. The lack of drop off shows weak diode connection. However there is a non-linear feature as the subcircuit does not allow voltages past 0.75V, instead outputs -0.5V. The overall shape is not expected and therefore the simulated results and this experimental data will not be valid.}}{14}{figure.caption.37}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:expnonlinear}{{14}{14}{Graph displaying experimental measurement of the non-linear component. The lack of drop off shows weak diode connection. However there is a non-linear feature as the subcircuit does not allow voltages past 0.75V, instead outputs -0.5V. The overall shape is not expected and therefore the simulated results and this experimental data will not be valid}{figure.caption.37}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces To show a complete return map with fractal structure, we need 20 times more sample points than previous RK4 solutions. This is to generate more peaks and so when we were generating experimental data, we could not produce a return map due to scarcity of peaks.}}{14}{figure.caption.39}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rmap}{{15}{14}{To show a complete return map with fractal structure, we need 20 times more sample points than previous RK4 solutions. This is to generate more peaks and so when we were generating experimental data, we could not produce a return map due to scarcity of peaks}{figure.caption.39}{}}
